(5795460, 841858, 66635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i>  I think you may have also overdid a bit of your processing as I see a bit of halo around the bird as well.  <br/> <br/>It is important to remember (and I always have to remind myself as well!) that it is not about the difficulty of the shot, but on what is delivered.   An analogy that I like to think about is that I don''t want to watch a musician play something that sounds like it is difficult to play, but rather I want to watch a musician play something effortlessly (even if the piece is difficult).<br/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, you''re right about that.  I don''t like that halo either.  Thanks to you and Dr. Achoo for the nice comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone:  I think you may have also overdid a bit of your processing as I see a bit of halo around the bird as well.   It is important to remember (and I always have to remind myself as well!) that it is not about the difficulty of the shot, but on what is delivered.   An analogy that I like to think about is that I don''t want to watch a musician play something that sounds like it is difficult to play, but rather I want to watch a musician play something effortlessly (even if the piece is difficult).   Well, you''re right about that.  I don''t like that halo either.  Thanks to you and Dr. Achoo for the nice comments.', '2010-01-04 14:43:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5795468, 841799, 30982, '<td valign="top">I moved into a cheap apartment in Tampa for a span of two months due to snafus in my assigment to my next job.  I had myself, a futon, a lawn chair, a laptop computer, two cats, and a coffee pot.  Came home from work one evening, settled into the lawn chair (which was inside, of course) and there was a knocking at the door.  Well no one really knew I was there, so I wondered who it could be.  Opened the door - no one was there - heard "Quack!" - looked down, and there were three Muscovy ducks just standing there, casual as can be, waiting to be fed.  Apparently the previous tenant would feed them.  They knocked almost every evening after that.  I had to buy Cheerios just for them.</td>', 'I moved into a cheap apartment in Tampa for a span of two months due to snafus in my assigment to my next job.  I had myself, a futon, a lawn chair, a laptop computer, two cats, and a coffee pot.  Came home from work one evening, settled into the lawn chair (which was inside, of course) and there was a knocking at the door.  Well no one really knew I was there, so I wondered who it could be.  Opened the door - no one was there - heard "Quack!" - looked down, and there were three Muscovy ducks just standing there, casual as can be, waiting to be fed.  Apparently the previous tenant would feed them.  They knocked almost every evening after that.  I had to buy Cheerios just for them.', '2010-01-04 14:48:19.000000', NULL, 0),
